        "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-106438: t=-2x gives y=-x². q-81831: A maps (a,b) to (b,-a), a clockwise quarter-turn; the upper-left vector becomes the steep upper-right vector in option 2. MA's final image includes the original vector as well, but depicts the same transformed vector. q-18372: c·d=-8 and |d|=√17. q-236734: p·q=x-2, so zero scalar projection requires x=2. q-32139: the determinant is -46; the displayed inverse gives (x,y)=(-4,9), satisfying both equations. q-114245: applying L'Hopital twice gives 1/(2x), hence 1/2. q-115526: differentiation gives -cos(x)sin(x), whose limit is zero. q-11858 and q-84947: the leftmost points are (-6,0) and (3,0). q-61906: six faces each have area 16 cm², totaling 96 cm². q-88454: 4^(3x)>0, so the roots are ±5 and their product is -25. The source's conjunction 'and' between the two factor equations should be 'or'; its separate-factor analysis and final answer remain correct. q-102416: the seventh root equals 1, so 3x+13=1 and x=-4. q-127844: 11 sin(27°)≈4.9939, rounding to 5n. q-146318: parallel vectors have zero cross product. q-48722: differentiating 4πr² gives 8πr. q-114168: evaluating 3cos(θ) between 0 and π/2 gives -3. No submitted-grade evidence or earlier answer was supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
