        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index",
        "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1.$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{3x+13} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[7]{3x+13})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 3x+13 & =1 \\\\ 3x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-4.$",
