        "problem": "The vector $v$ has magnitude $12,$ the vector $w$ has magnitude $10,$ and the angle between the vectors is ${0}^{∘}.$ What is $v\\times w?$",
        "worked_solution": "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nSince the angle between $v$ and $w$ is ${0}^{∘},$ our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $v\\times w=0.$",
